      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's an updated draft memo:\n\nSubject: Maintaining a Healthy and Ergonomic Workspace\n\nAs we continue to work from our remote locations, we want to remind everyone of the importance of maintaining a healthy and ergonomic workspace. This can help prevent injuries such as wrist and back pain. To achieve this, please follow these guidelines for your workstation setup:\n\n- Position your monitor directly in front of you, at a distance of 3-4 feet, and at a height that allows you to gaze slightly downward.\n- Position your chair so that your feet are flat on the floor or on a footrest, with your knees at or below hip level.\n- Place your keyboard directly in front of your body, with your wrists straight and elbows at a 90-degree angle. Keep your hands in a neutral position, with your wrists not extended or flexed.\n- Place your mouse close to your body and at the same height as your keyboard.\n- Take regular breaks (every 30-60 minutes) to stand up, stretch, and move around. We encourage \"micro-breaks\" of 5-10 minutes, where you can walk around, stretch, and relax.\n- Try to work in 90-minute increments, followed by a 10-",
